Configure Logstash Authentication

Update the logstash's configuration file /etc/logstash/conf.d/logstash.conf

Add 2 lines on the Elasticsearch's Output plugging:
user =>'elastic'
password =>'password'
systemctl restart logstash

#use the password you keyed-in in the previous steps
#in our case is cfglog.conf as mentioned in the handbook

*********************************************************
Configure Filebeat Authentication

Update /etc/filebeat/filebeat.yml

#since - type: log is deprecated, we now use Filestream input block instead:
---------------------------------------------
filebeat.inputs:

- type: filestream
  id: messages-log
enabled : true
paths:
- /var/log/messages
tags: ["Messages-logs"]

- type: filestream
enabled : true
id: secure-log
paths:
- /var/log/secure
tags: ["Secure-logs"]

- type: filestream
enabled : true
id: suricata-log
paths:
- /var/log/suricata/eve.json
tags: ["Suricata-logs"]

 ### Parsers configuration
  #### JSON configuration

  parsers:
     ndjson:
     keys_under_root: true # the keys (decoded JSON fields of the log line) are copied to the top level of the output document alongside message and @timestamp instead of these fields get nested inside a json object, when parsing.
     add_error_key: true # if JSON parsing encounters an error, Filebeat adds an error.message field to the event instead of silently dropping/pasing the raw line -- critical for catching malformed log lines.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#if you are still using the old configuration, you should allow deprecated use until jumping to 9.x at which point it will be fully removed:

filebeat.inputs:
- type: log
enabled : true
#to be abe to still use type log:
allow_deprecated_use: true
paths:
- /var/log/messages
tags: ["Messages-logs"]
- type: log
paths:
- /var/log/secure
tags: ["Secure-logs"]
- type: log
paths:
- /var/log/suricata/eve.json
tags: ["Suricata-logs"]

